  "problem": "In a microchip factory, each chip is tested for defects before being packaged. On average, $6$ out of every $200$ chips are defective. The chips are tested one by one until a defective chip is found. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability that a defective chip will be found before testing the $5$th chip is{{field-1}}.",
